author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Finishing an item with links, evidence, resolution and release is expressible as one governed act that costs one bootstrap and returns one receipt; The act is atomic: an interruption leaves either the whole completion recorded or none of it, and no state where an item is closed but still claimed is reachable through the prescribed path; The record identifies the constituent mutations as one act, so a later reader reconstructs the single intent rather than seven timestamp-adjacent entries; The evidence flags accepted at completion are the same names and the same value grammar as the evidence flags accepted at creation, with no second spelling for the same concept; The composed form is never the only form: each constituent verb remains individually callable and unchanged for callers that link evidence incrementally"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: 92
resolution: "Atomic completion primitive and pm item complete command ship evidence update, governed close, and claim release in one durable transaction with exposed lock TTL/wait controls and history-first recovery that never releases a later claimant."
expected_result: "Packages and agents can complete tracked work in one governed, replay-safe operation without partial lifecycle state or lost claim ownership."
actual_result: "Forward, forced-failure, crash-before-journal, later-reclaim, and resume tests prove committed state, exact compensation restoration, and preservation of later ownership; focused tests pass 60/60 and the full 6,864-test repository suite holds 100/100/100/100 coverage."
